S_ALL.IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y': SUPPORTED (hint mapping; dw_1393 uses identical predicate).\n- Filter \"> 0 total units\" → SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS > 0: SUPPORTED (dw_1393 precedent).\n- Filter \"Mathematics department\" → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics': SUPPORTED (hint mapping; column_concept_department_name decision guide: \"Filtering subjects by department in catalog or summary analysis → use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\").\n- Grouping keys ACADEMIC_YEAR + DEPARTMENT_NAME: SUPPORTED (hint mapping).\n- Measure CLEARING_COST_COLLECTOR avg/stddev → SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT: SUPPORTED (only table with this column).\n- Filter degree-granting → SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y': SUPPORTED.\n- Exclude Political Science → SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '17': SUPPORTED (hint maps exclusion to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; dw_2559 documents Political Science = Course 17).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"subjects offered in the current term\" → `IS_CURRENT_TERM = 'Y'` on ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (hint: \"current term: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.IS_CURRENT_TERM\"). Not IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR (that maps to \"offered this year\" wording used in other metrics like dw_1471).\n- \"Mathematics department\" → DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' in the catalog table (hint mapping).\n- \"excluding the Political Science department\" → hint explicitly anchors to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, i.e. code '17' (Course 17 per dw_2559's description).\n- \"its associated administrative department (including only departments that grant degrees...)\" → plural \"departments\" defines the population over which clearing-cost stats are aggregated: SIS_DEPARTMENT (IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y', code≠'17') joined to SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT. Since SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT holds one row per administrative department, a per-single-department STDDEV would be degenerate (NULL); the plural filter wording indicates one aggregate over the filtered department set — matching dw_2224's pattern of computing clearing-cost statistics over a filtered degree-granting department population.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- Same-shape precedent (year+dept VARIANCE/STDDEV of TOTAL_UNITS with IS_CURRENT_TERM='Y', TOTAL_UNITS>0, Mathematics, joining CC+TERMS_ALL+SUMMARY on TERM_CODE): **1 — dw_1393** (exact join structure and filters).\n- Clearing-cost-collector AVG/VARIANCE/STDDEV precedents: **1 — dw_2224** (SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y', department exclusions by code).\n- VARIANCE/STDDEV of catalog TOTAL_UNITS by year precedents: dw_1023, dw_41 (use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS — not the hint-selected source here).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: consumed by dozens of metrics for catalog-attribute analysis (units, grading, HGN, offering flags); joins terms, departments, rooms, instructors.\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY: used for enrollment/unit statistics by department/term (dw_1393, dw_3644, dw_1212 etc.).\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: term enrichment/current-term filtering (dw_1393, dw_41).\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT: degree-granting and school filters in department-scoped metrics (dw_2224, dw_2151, dw_1350...).\n- SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT: department contact/clearing-cost statistics (dw_2224, dw_1427, dw_1833).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph neighbors ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: semantic_get ✓ (columns), graph via search descriptions ✓\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY: semantic_get ✓\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT: semantic_get ✓\n- SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT: semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph neighbors ✓\n- dw_1393, dw_2224, dw_1023, dw_41: semantic_get (full SQL) ✓; other metrics: descriptions reviewed via search ✓\n- concept_department_dimension, column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name: semantic_get ✓; remaining concepts/column-concepts: descriptions reviewed ✓\n- mysql_query attempted 4× — all failed with access-denied (environment issue); ver